<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">9 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 9 April, from 193 to 2003.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/danube" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/danube.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">193 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,833 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Danube legions proclaim Septimius Severus emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After the murder of Pertinax, the legions at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carnuntum">Carnuntum</a> hailed their governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/septimius-severus">Septimius Severus</a> as emperor. He marched on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, defeated his rivals and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/severan-dynasty">Severan dynasty</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/septimius-severus">Septimius Severus</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1241">1241 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">785 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mongols defeat a Polish and German army at Legnica</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A Mongol force under Baidar and Kadan crushed the army of Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-the-pious">Henry II the Pious</a>, who was killed. Two days later the main Mongol army destroyed the Hungarians at Mohi.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1388">1388 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">638 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Glarus defeats a Habsburg army at the Battle of Näfels</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The men of Glarus, helped by Schwyz and their allies of the Old Swiss Confederacy, defeated a much larger army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>. The victory secured the independence of Glarus from Habsburg rule and is commemorated every April.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-nafels">Battle of Näfels</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1438">1438 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">588 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Council of Ferrara opens under Pope Eugene IV</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-eugene-iv">Pope Eugene IV</a> presided over the first solemn session of the council he had moved from Basel to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferrara">Ferrara</a>, attended by the Eastern Roman Emperor and the Patriarch of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>. It debated the issues of the East–West Schism.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-basel">Council of Basel</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-eugene-iv">Pope Eugene IV</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ecumenical-patriarch-of-constantinople">Ecumenical Patriarch of Constantinople</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1682">1682 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">344 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">La Salle claims the Mississippi basin for France</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Reaching the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rene-robert-cavelier-sieur-de-la-salle">René-Robert Cavelier de La Salle</a> claimed its whole drainage basin for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a> and named it <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> sold the territory to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> in 1803.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/new-france">New France</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1865">1865 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">161 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lee surrenders to Grant at Appomattox Court House</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-e-lee">Robert E. Lee</a> surrendered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/army-of-northern-virginia">Army of Northern Virginia</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ulysses-s-grant">Ulysses S. Grant</a>. Other Confederate forces followed in the weeks after, bringing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a> to an end.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1940">1940 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">86 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Germany invades Denmark and Norway</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">German forces struck both neutral states in Operation Weserübung. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> yielded within hours, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>, aided by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, fought on for two months, giving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> vital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea">North Sea</a> and Atlantic bases.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea">North Sea</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1945">1945 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Dietrich Bonhoeffer is executed at Flossenbürg</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Lutheran pastor and theologian Dietrich Bonhoeffer was hanged on Hitler's orders for his links to the resistance. He died a month before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>'s surrender.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2003">2003 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">23 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Baghdad falls and Saddam's statue is pulled down</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">As US troops entered central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>, a statue of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saddam-hussein">Saddam Hussein</a> in Firdos Square was toppled with the help of a Marine vehicle. The images marked the regime's collapse, though years of insurgency followed.</p></div></li></ol>
